WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.790 --> 00:00:06.589
Exactly, we don't let our friends,
or people who come here to build,

2
00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:12.011
build shacks, put up metal sheets,
wood, that sort of thing.

3
00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:14.946
Because it makes the place
look really run-down.

4
00:00:15.956 --> 00:00:18.827
It's left without conditions.
And if a fire breaks out,

5
00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:23.089
if it catches fire,
the blame always falls on us.

6
00:00:23.173 --> 00:00:26.114
"See? No proper conditions, none of that."

7
00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:32.490
And we said: "No, no, let's build
with blocks, masonry, as they say."

8
00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:39.214
We build with that,
to avoid an ugly appearance,

9
00:00:39.503 --> 00:00:40.915
because it degrades the city.

10
00:00:41.386 --> 00:00:47.586
When there are metal sheets and pallets,
the place looks bad, really run-down.

11
00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:52.180
But when the place is built
with blocks or bricks,

12
00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:55.904
nicely done, and then with a good finish,

13
00:00:56.342 --> 00:00:59.752
the place will look nice and tidy,
really pretty. There's no doubt.

14
00:00:59.836 --> 00:01:04.828
But the City Council
and the IHRU don't want that,

15
00:01:05.375 --> 00:01:09.610
because they know that when we do it,
the place will look nice.

16
00:01:10.276 --> 00:01:12.787
When it's nicely plastered,

17
00:01:12.897 --> 00:01:18.670
with the door and window nicely painted,
the house painted, it looks good.

18
00:01:18.861 --> 00:01:24.160
They can't say: "No,
look how bad it is, grey and all."

19
00:01:24.244 --> 00:01:29.217
No, no, we want the place
to be really nice and tidy.

20
00:01:29.427 --> 00:01:31.380
We just live in fear.

21
00:01:33.489 --> 00:01:38.382
We're afraid to do things.
Because, if they let us,

22
00:01:38.733 --> 00:01:42.512
look: we'd take care of our house fronts,
we'd take care of the street.

23
00:01:42.596 --> 00:01:47.115
We want to fix up the street,
to really build,

24
00:01:47.199 --> 00:01:52.773
to make the road properly,
because it's covered in mud.

25
00:01:52.927 --> 00:01:55.181
We live in fear. What time will they come?

26
00:01:55.265 --> 00:01:57.943
Tomorrow the machine comes,
another day it comes.

27
00:01:58.027 --> 00:02:03.180
We live with that fear: "Do I invest,
and then they tear it down?"

28
00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:07.511
With that kind of fear.

29
00:02:07.801 --> 00:02:10.932
But no, now we've chosen
differently: "No, no, no.

30
00:02:11.141 --> 00:02:15.420
Let's make our houses look nice and take
care of our neighbourhood, Penajóia.

31
00:02:15.504 --> 00:02:20.422
Everything has to... Everyone has
to fix up their house and build,

32
00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:23.077
paint, so it looks nice."

33
00:02:23.161 --> 00:02:26.638
That's why, I don't know if you can see:
it's all starting to look like this,

34
00:02:26.722 --> 00:02:30.325
they're adding insulation,
so it looks nice. That's how we want it.

35
00:02:30.409 --> 00:02:36.261
We want a peaceful neighbourhood.
We want police here in the neighbourhood.

36
00:02:36.345 --> 00:02:40.286
We want it to be like you, who come here
and feel welcome in the neighbourhood,

37
00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:44.784
without any problem... And we don't
have any problems here. They know it.

38
00:02:45.194 --> 00:02:47.465
The IHRU knows, the City Council knows.

39
00:02:47.575 --> 00:02:50.606
They come here, walk around
the neighbourhood, do everything.

40
00:02:50.916 --> 00:02:54.073
There's no threat here,
there's no problem.

41
00:02:54.157 --> 00:02:58.515
They make up the problem:
something happens somewhere else,

42
00:02:58.599 --> 00:03:01.950
and they pin it on the neighbourhood,
to punish Penajóia.

43
00:03:03.653 --> 00:03:07.006
But when a problem happens,
it's not here that it happens.

44
00:03:07.256 --> 00:03:09.727
If it's going to happen,
it happens everywhere.

45
00:03:10.676 --> 00:03:14.293
Even in the city,
there's some problem, it always happens.

46
00:03:14.377 --> 00:03:17.628
But we want them to leave us in peace.

47
00:03:19.178 --> 00:03:25.169
They don't find a solution. All we want...
If they let us... What do they want?

48
00:03:25.359 --> 00:03:28.930
Do we want to build the road?

49
00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:33.065
We'll do it.
We'll all get together, pool the money,

50
00:03:33.436 --> 00:03:36.726
and lay the asphalt, whatever it takes.

51
00:03:37.056 --> 00:03:40.527
We just need their permission,
which they never give us.

52
00:03:40.717 --> 00:03:45.568
Because they want us to look like this,
always run-down,

53
00:03:46.558 --> 00:03:52.160
looking bad, so they can make the TV news.

54
00:03:53.179 --> 00:03:58.750
That's what they want. Because if they
didn't, they'd have helped us already.

55
00:03:59.595 --> 00:04:03.187
They'd have put in water, we'd have
electricity, we'd have none of this.

56
00:04:03.424 --> 00:04:04.914
But people start talking,

57
00:04:04.998 --> 00:04:08.830
they talk, talk, talk, talk,
and many start saying things about us,

58
00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:14.993
without really knowing the true
reason people are here in Penajóia.

59
00:04:15.984 --> 00:04:18.955
In other words, everyone knows:
there's no housing.

60
00:04:20.086 --> 00:04:24.318
You can't afford the rent, because wages,

61
00:04:25.549 --> 00:04:28.500
as I keep saying,
aren't wages, they're a tip.

62
00:04:29.366 --> 00:04:31.542
They don't even cover the rent.

63
00:04:31.833 --> 00:04:34.774
If you manage to pay the rent,
there's nothing left for food.

64
00:04:35.176 --> 00:04:37.094
If you eat, you don't pay the phone bill,

65
00:04:37.178 --> 00:04:42.212
or your travel pass, or feed your child,
or pay for their school.

66
00:04:42.322 --> 00:04:45.435
All Portuguese people know that.
All of them.

67
00:04:45.786 --> 00:04:51.080
That's why we need help.
We need them to help us and work with us.

68
00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:55.461
Because, just as we came here to work,

69
00:04:55.545 --> 00:04:57.668
because Portugal needs labour,

70
00:04:57.752 --> 00:05:01.769
we need money to help our families,
our homeland,

71
00:05:01.853 --> 00:05:07.065
to build a better life.
Now, you come here, you go into a house...

72
00:05:08.156 --> 00:05:12.747
Wages are 800 euros,
now they're 900 euros, 900 euros.

73
00:05:13.477 --> 00:05:19.829
And a one-bedroom flat, a one-bedroom
or a studio, for 1,000 euros.

74
00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:23.996
How is that possible?
What are immigrants supposed to live on?

75
00:05:24.687 --> 00:05:28.479
They come hoping to help
their families back home,

76
00:05:28.563 --> 00:05:31.622
to save a little money
to build their own house,

77
00:05:31.732 --> 00:05:34.650
but they can't, they can't.

78
00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:40.374
Not even people who live here can, on
the wages they get here. It's very little.

79
00:05:40.458 --> 00:05:42.309
And now the rent is going up,

80
00:05:42.393 --> 00:05:45.938
electricity is going up, water
is going up, fuel, everything is going up.

81
00:05:46.022 --> 00:05:48.289
And wages?
They're not enough for anything.
